{"id":"resp_a32ee062df2b5513","created_at":1795604603,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_bf2efe61544ee2b9","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce assessment JSON with fields: assessment, issues, questions, gap_review.\n\nWe must evaluate candidate SHACL shape for TRF-035 clause 4.1.1: It defines ruleLength, classificationSocietyRuleLength, classificationSociety. Need to ensure obligations: Represent L as ship's rule length used by classification society. The shape captures ruleLength (nltl:ruleLength) as QuantityValue with numericValue decimal and unit M. classificationSocietyRuleLength also same. classificationSociety string.\n\nPotential issues: Are there constraints linking ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength? Requirement says L shall be taken as ship's rule length used by classification society. Could interpret that ruleLength must equal classificationSocietyRuleLength? The shape treats them independent, no equality constraint. Might be missing constraint that they are equal or at least consistent. But representation may be okay: ruleLength is ship's rule length; classificationSocietyRuleLength is as recorded by society—could be same value but not enforced. The requirement may require both present, not necessarily equal, just record. Possibly need to ensure both present. Already present minCount=1 maxCount=1 enforce existence.\n\nPotential missing datatype for classificationSociety string? Already xsd:string.\n\nPotential missing unit for ruleLength? Provided hasValue M ensures unit is correct. That matches requirement \"canonical metre unit\". Good.\n\nPotential missing targetClass? Already nltl:ship.\n\nPotential missing shape for L equals classificationSocietyRuleLength? Might be considered a material requirement. Evaluate if representation must enforce equality? The clause: “L shall be taken as the ship’s rule length used by the classification society.” Means that whenever L is used elsewhere, it refers to that value. In SHACL, we might need to assert that ex:ShipRuleLengthShape defines both properties but does not link them. However the shape could be acceptable as representation of the two distinct properties.\n\nIssue could be that property nltl:classificationSocietyRuleLength is defined as QuantityValue with unit M, but the source mapping may indicate it's a numeric quantity (length). That matches.\n\nPotential missing minCount for classificationSocietyRuleLength? Already there.\n\nCheck for range constraints: classificationSocietyRuleLength sh:node includes numericValue and unit, but no datatype for numericValue? It has xsd:decimal. Good.\n\nCheck for sh:property block closing brackets: shape syntax seems correct.\n\nPotential issues with prefixes: used ex: prefix but not declared? ex is declared. Good.\n\nPotential missing sh:targetObjectsOf? Not needed.\n\nNow review gap_review: There are G1-G5. We must assess each material? Gap_review items need id, material (bool), why. Material indicates whether gap is material (affects compliance). Likely G1, G2, G3, G4 are source gaps due to unresolved citation; may be material because missing source text impacts completeness of representation. Could be considered material: need to resolve source citations to verify requirements. So we mark material true with why.\n\nG5 is missing document for UR P0; also material.\n\nBut according to instructions: If any gap is material, must be a question? Gap_review must be filled with material boolean; if material true, maybe need a question? The schema expects gap_review array with id, material, why. So we provide material true and explain.\n\nNow questions: any missing info? Possibly need to ask about equality constraint. Could add a question: Is there requirement that ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength must be equal? Provide missing mapping.\n\nWe need to include in questions array entries with missing, why, kind, reference? Provide reference to clause? Use maybe \"missing\" field description. Provide kind \"source\" or \"schema\". This is a missing mapping; we can ask.\n\nNow issues: Since we need at least one issue if assessment REJECT. But we can APPROVE if all obligations satisfied and gaps are material? Approval requires no current/prior issue or material question, all changes SUPPORTED and every supplied gap explicitly nonmaterial. But we have material gaps, so cannot APPROVE. Could set assessment \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\". That requires at least one material question or unresolved change/gap. So we must include a question. Also need gap_review entries marked material true.\n\nThus assessment = \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\".\n\nProvide issues array empty (no code defects). Provide questions array with at least one asking about equality constraint. Provide gap_review for each G1..G5 with material true/false? To trigger human review, we need at least one material question. We have that.\n\nNow construct JSON.\n\nIssue fields require description, evidence, location, suggestion; none needed.\n\nQuestion fields: missing (string), why, kind (source or schema), reference optional, evidence optional. Provide missing: \"Equality between ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength not enforced\". why: \"Clause 4.1.1 defines L as rule length used by classification society; representation should ensure both values are identical\". kind: \"schema\". reference could be clause \"TRF-035 | 4.1.1\". Provide evidence maybe E331 which contains excerpt. Use evidence array with \"E331\". Provide location not needed for question.\n\ngap_review entries: for each id G1..G5, material true, why \"Source citation not resolved; required to verify completeness of requirement\". Provide.\n\nNow build JSON. Ensure no extra fields.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_b52a1dd45092c701","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"{\n  \"assessment\": \"HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n  \"issues\": [],\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"missing\": \"Enforcement of equality between nltl:ruleLength and nltl:classificationSocietyRuleLength\",\n      \"why\": \"Clause 4.1.1 states that L shall be taken as the ship's rule length used by the classification society, implying that the two recorded lengths must be identical. The current SHACL shape defines both properties independently without a constraint linking them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"schema\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"E331\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gap_review\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G1\",\n      \"material\": true,\n      \"why\": \"Section 10 reference is missing or ambiguous; required to confirm the full textual requirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G2\",\n      \"material\": true,\n      \"why\": \"Section 3 reference is missing or ambiguous; needed to validate clause context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G3\",\n      \"material\": true,\n      \"why\": \"Table 3 reference is ambiguous with multiple matches; essential for confirming numeric parameters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G4\",\n      \"material\": true,\n      \"why\": \"Table 6 reference is ambiguous with multiple matches; needed for complete representation of load cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"G5\",\n      \"material\": true,\n      \"why\": \"Document UR P0 is reported as missing; source material required for full requirement coverage.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":n